What are Cleanroom FFUs and Filters?
Fan Filter Units (FFUs) are critical components designed to maintain ultra-clean environments by circulating purified air through HEPA (High-Efficiency Particulate Air) or ULPA (Ultra-Low Penetration Air) filters. These systems create unidirectional airflow in cleanrooms, removing airborne contaminants to levels as low as 0.12 microns. Modern FFUs are increasingly integrated with smart monitoring and energy-efficient designs, making them indispensable for industries where even minimal particulate contamination can compromise product quality.
